WEBVTT

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:05.550
Come on.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.190
Yet another transfer.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.030
It's what the parents wanted.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.570
We have more dangerous missions lately,

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.610
and there is severe criticism 
against the Toji as well.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.630
How did she feel about it?

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:27.190
She seemed to want to stay,
 but you're just students, after all.

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:31.390
Your parents have to agree to it.
Otherwise, you have to hand in your okatana.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.710
<b>Absence Permission Slip</b>

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:36.080
You're off to Kamakura 
again next week, right?

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.970
I'm sure it will be tough, but do your best.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.800
I will, thank you.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.650
Please excuse me.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.600
<b>Father</b>

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.170
Father?

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:22.900
<b>Katana Maidens</b>

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:29.370
<b>Episode 14  Family Scene</b>

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.420
I'm home.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:30.910
Huh? Mai-oneechan!

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.290
You're not staying in the dorms today?

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:36.690
No, something came up. Where's Mio?

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.340
Mio-oneechan would be...

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:41.710
<b>Potato
 Chips</b>

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.710
Welcome back, Mai-nee.

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:46.690
Don't "welcome back" me. You're lazing
 about in your uniform again.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:50.100
I'll change after I'm done with this.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.940
You're getting it all wrinkled.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.270
Come on, take it off.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.560
Jeez, it's such a pain...

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.820
Father and the others will be 
home soon, so behave properly.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.400
Huh? Dad is coming home?

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.470
He was actually in Japan?

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:07.870
Does that mean Mom is coming home, too?

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.670
Yes, she is with him.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:11.440
That's unusual.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.910
When was the last time we were all together?

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:17.990
Let's see... Not since 
Shiori's birthday, I think?

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.640
They've been pretty busy, it seems.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.140
Hey! Don't eat standing up!

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.210
Yes, yes.

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:27.740
Only say "yes" once.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.010
What?

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:35.520
Fussing over details like that 
is why you don't have a boyfriend.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.690
That is none of your concern!

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:43.440
Welcome home, Father, Mother.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:44.900
Welcome home!

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:45.940
Welcome back.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:48.200
We're home.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.410
Mai, we need to speak with you.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.280
Yes, sir.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.250
Mai, we want you to leave Minoseki Academy.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:02.100
Your mother and I have decided 
on a new school for you.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.090
You can transfer there immediately.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.990
That's not what you said before.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:09.580
You said I could do what I wanted 
until I graduated from high school.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:13.260
Surely you understand that the 
circumstances have changed.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.650
The number of Toji getting hurt during 
missions has been increasing, hasn't it?

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:21.190
Even you've been in a fair amount of danger.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.440
That's true, but...

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:30.410
Magorokukanemoto here chose me, 
and I chose to become a Toji.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:32.990
I am prepared for what that means.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:35.700
You shouldn't say such frivolous things!

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:47.050
Mai, don't forget, you are 
a member of this family, too.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:52.180
Is it that bad for the reputation of 
the Yanase family to have a Toji in it?

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:53.590
Mai...

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:58.300
I'm sorry. I went too far.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:04:59.850
You too, dear.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.860
Okay, then. We'll give you some time.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:06.730
Think it over well.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:08.810
Yes, sir.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.360
<b>Etou Kanami</b>

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:26.480
<i>Headquarters to all units on guard:</i>

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:29.030
<i>take action as soon as 
you capture the target.</i>

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:31.130
<i>Don't let it contaminate anything else!</i>

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:35.510
Sakuma!

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:06.670
She took down an aradama that
 powerful with a single blow?

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:15.950
Who was that?

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:22.080
You make the most delicious 
breakfasts, Mai-oneechan.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.900
I'd rather have toast, though.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.170
Stop complaining and eat.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:28.500
Yes, yes.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:29.220
Only say...

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:30.210
..."yes" once.

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:34.790
Morning, Dad!

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:35.780
Morning.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.280
Is Mom still asleep?

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:43.290
Yes, we were pretty busy for a while.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:46.430
You even have to work on a Sunday?

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:47.470
Yes.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:48.750
What about breakfast?

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:51.700
Dad always just has coffee.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.670
Then, I will get your coffee right away.

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:56.270
No, I don't have time.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.870
Shibata, bring the car around.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.330
Certainly, sir.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:06.990
Mai, I need you to get ready to leave, too.

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:16.560
Where are we?

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.070
Up until recently, this place was known as

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:21.950
the Special Rare Metals Research 
and Development Organization.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.340
I'm sure you've at least heard of it.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:30.150
Yes, but wasn't it closed when the structure 
of the Sword Administration changed?

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:33.590
Only as a state-owned independent 
administrative corporation.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:38.160
We provided it with funding and re-opened it

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:42.800
as a private research institution, the Special
 Rare Metals Utilization Research Institute.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:44.080
Utilization?

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.190
That's right.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:48.100
It is a facility searching for 
uses for tamahagane steel

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.970
beyond just okatana.

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:55.360
What is this?

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:59.280
Here, they are currently conducting 
research to extract energy

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.870
from the netherworld with tamahagane 
steel as an intermediary.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.290
Is something like that even possible?

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.170
Theoretically.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:13.750
Tamahagane steel is a metal that can affect 
the netherworld while existing in this world.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.840
By using that characteristic,

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.710
we can blur the boundary between 
this world and the netherworld

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:22.420
and make a substance emerge in this 
world that has never existed before.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:23.920
If this becomes possible,

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:26.260
we could acquire an 
inexhaustible energy source

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:29.690
that ignores the conventional 
laws of physics.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.940
Pardon me, but you are?

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.790
Oh, forgive me.

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:38.580
I am Kohagura Kimitake. I serve 
as the chief of research here.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.720
And I'm his wife, Jacqueline.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:41.820
Nice to meet you.

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:43.930
Likewise.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.400
Kohagura? Then...

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:49.710
Yes, we are Ellen's mom and dad.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:50.800
Huh?!

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:52.910
Are you surprised?

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:55.360
Friedman-san!

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:58.150
It's been a while, Mai-kun.

00:08:58.150 --> 00:08:59.790
What are you doing here?

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:02.260
Your father asked me to come.

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:06.720
I'm serving as honorary 
advisor to this institute.

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:08.000
My father did?

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.390
That's exactly right.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:14.830
But you must really have some 
kind of connection with my family

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:18.870
to be acquainted with my granddaughter, 
 my daughter, and her husband.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:22.280
I've heard a lot about you, Mai-mai.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:23.910
Mai-mai?

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:29.660
Ellen-san, their daughter, 
likes to call me that.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:31.500
I see.

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:35.290
<i>Chief, the proximity reaction 
experiment is finished.</i>

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:38.530
<i>I'd like to move on to data analysis.</i>

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:41.920
Got it. Please return the 
noro to the storage area.

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:43.020
Noro?

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.600
What's wrong, Mai?

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:55.550
What experiment is that?

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:58.560
We are observing the reaction that occurs

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.820
when tamahagane steel is 
brought close to noro.

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:03.990
You use noro here in your experiments?

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.200
Well, yes, we do.

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:13.700
You seem to be exceedingly 
afraid of noro, Mai-kun.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:17.570
I am not afraid of it. I respect it.

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:21.960
You were the one who taught 
me to do so, Friedman-san.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:27.600
That's true. I did tell you it was better 
for it to be separated and enshrined.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:32.560
But while that may be a better way,
 perhaps it is not the best.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:36.250
Noro has a consciousness and will.

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:40.870
Not to mention, we have Princess 
Tagitsu and Nene as examples.

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:45.070
So you're saying that the noro
does not wish to be enshrined?

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:48.450
It's much better than just leaving it alone.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:52.850
But I'm saying maybe there 
is an even better way.

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:54.750
An even better way?

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:57.710
I've been wondering if the noro's impurity

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.750
is actually loneliness.

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:02.460
Loneliness?

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:05.570
Enshrining noro seems to be nothing more

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:10.210
than just a gesture with the intent 
to forget it while appearing admirable.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.720
Just like the festival in the village.

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:16.510
Why do noro feel so lonely?

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:19.590
They seek the tamahagane steel.

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:20.870
The other part of itself

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:23.730
that it was forcibly separated 
from by the hand of man.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:27.650
That experiment is to demonstrate 
that noro's impurity

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:31.700
will be cleansed by bringing it 
closer to the tamahagane steel.

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:33.970
In fact, a decrease in the impurity

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:36.870
has been observed in proportion 
to the distance and time.

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:40.640
It almost sounds like a 
child who feels relieved

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.030
by being held by its mother, don't you think?

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.130
But...

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:46.510
Right. Unfortunately,

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:50.240
there is no way to recombine the 
noro with the tamahagane steel.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:54.190
We call that one Nemo.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.270
Nemo?

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:58.190
Lonely Little Nemo.

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:02.660
You know, I would like to hear its voice.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:05.510
What is it that it really wants?

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:09.460
Is there some place more comfortable 
for it than being enshrined?

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:11.850
So it can tell me all of that.

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:17.260
I decided to fund this place 
after I heard that story.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:21.280
If possible, I would like for 
you to help us in the future.

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:23.850
I...

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:27.960
Mai-mai!

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.630
Long time no see!

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:32.890
E-Ellen-chan?

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.650
So, are you on a mission?

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.830
Yes, since there have been

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:47.910
consecutive incidents where 
noro have been stolen recently,

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.780
we are on extreme alert.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:53.280
But Minoseki is closer to this location.

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:56.400
Well, when Grandpa heard 
about the security issue,

00:12:56.400 --> 00:13:00.900
he thought we could get the family together 
again after so long. So he nominated me.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:02.830
He tends to mix his business 
and his personal life.

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:06.640
That phrase doesn't really have 
a good meaning in Japanese.

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:09.170
Anyway, what are you wearing?

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:14.450
This is a present from my dad.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:16.720
It's not really suitable for a mission,

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:20.790
but I figured I would wear 
it where he could see me.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.470
So that's the reason.

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:24.210
It looks very nice on you.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:26.020
Thank you.

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:31.110
Your dad is so wonderful, Mai-mai.

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:34.450
W-Wonderful?

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:39.870
If this place closed down, my parents 
would've be out on the streets.

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:44.420
My grandpa is rich, so he could have 
helped them if it came to that,

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:46.790
but it's not good to mix 
business and personal matters.

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:49.530
That's a bit different from
what you were saying earlier.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:54.470
Why do you think your dad funded this place?

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:59.720
Because he thought tamahagane steel 
research would be profitable?

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:02.030
Not quite.

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:03.840
If it had been profitable research,

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:06.800
then it wouldn't have almost 
gone under in the first place.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:07.710
Then...

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:11.830
If we can clear away the impurities 
of noro with tamahagane steel,

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.240
then Toji might not be necessary anymore.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:18.210
And you won't have to be in danger, either.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.680
That's why he'll do whatever it takes.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:24.680
At least, I think that's what he's thinking.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:26.250
You're overthinking things.

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:28.220
You think so?

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:32.430
My family is unique.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.400
My mom, dad, and even grandpa

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:37.860
are people who have dedicated 
their lives to research.

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:40.660
We may be all together 
like this at the moment,

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:44.140
but that's a pretty rare occurrence.

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:46.530
Much like my family.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:51.590
But Dad gives me presents on my birthday.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:54.180
Even if he can't be there in person,

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:58.340
every year, without fail, I get new clothes.

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.080
Then that dress...

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.250
Yes.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:05.300
It is Kohagura Ellen's 16th birthday present.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.470
It's pretty childish, huh?

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:10.760
Honestly, it's not really my style.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:13.050
He doesn't really get it.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:16.330
But even still...

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:22.240
This dress is full to the 
brim with Dad's love.

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:24.930
That much I can be sure of.

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.920
What about you, Mai-mai?

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:30.810
I...

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:37.450
What is this?

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:41.840
This is an image taken late 
last night in Aichi Prefecture.

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:45.710
Could this be the person 
who's stealing the noro?

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.810
You're pretty in the know.

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:50.830
Guess I can't stop people 
from talking after all.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.580
This person has an okatana.

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:57.630
So this is why you've been hiding this?

00:15:58.190 --> 00:15:59.570
What's that mean?

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:03.430
The big shots haven't abandoned the 
idea that this is an inside job.

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:06.470
Don't go talking about what 
you've seen and heard here.

00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:10.070
The credibility of the 
Administration would sink, too.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:12.310
If it's a secret, then why...?

00:16:12.310 --> 00:16:16.070
She's right. Why are you 
showing us this image?

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.130
About that...

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.180
Do you recognize this swordsmanship?

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:26.290
That looks like Shidou-san?

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:28.590
So you think so, too?

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:04.280
What's going on?!

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:08.240
An okatana!

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:10.980
Then the noro thief is...

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:13.330
Yes, a Toji.

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:15.750
Ellen, what are you doing?

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:17.910
I'm sorry, Dad!

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:19.670
I'll sew it back on later.

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:25.280
Dad, Mom, Grandpa... I'm off.

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:27.360
Wait, I'm coming, too.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:28.060
Mai!

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:34.880
I'm sorry, Father.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:37.400
I am still a Toji, after all!

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:39.110
Mai!

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:41.200
Yanase-san...

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:46.430
Even if we were to go, too, 
we would only be in the way.

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:51.680
Stop!

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:54.580
We will cut you down if you resist!

00:17:56.710 --> 00:18:00.000
Seems we don't need to hold back, Mai-mai.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.050
Indeed.

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:14.300
Mai...

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:18.980
Goodness! They are
 quite surprising, aren't they?

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:25.010
Children grow up big and 
strong before we realize it.

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:27.530
Far more than their parents think.

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:29.440
Yes.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:33.760
What should a parent do in 
that situation, I wonder?

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:39.630
Ellen-chan, we must finish this.

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:43.840
We won't let you go any farther.

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:52.600
Ellen-chan!

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:56.770
I'm fine! Please, go after her!

00:18:57.850 --> 00:18:58.650
Right.

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:10.490
I see. So Nemo is gone, then.

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:12.690
We're sorry.

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:16.690
No, it's thanks to you 
both that no one got hurt.

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:18.250
You did well.

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:20.300
Grandpa...

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:21.260
Ellen.

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:22.960
Dad...

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:27.840
I'm sorry. I ruined your present.

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:29.090
Dad?

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:33.520
Your father isn't upset about the dress.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.930
All that matters is that you're safe.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:37.710
Okay.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:40.940
Now it's your turn, Mai-kun.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.310
Father...

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:46.670
I'm sorry for what I said yesterday.

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:49.910
It doesn't have to do with the family.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:53.110
You are our precious daughter.

00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:55.410
I don't want you to forget that.

00:19:55.990 --> 00:19:57.660
Father...

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:06.050
Mai-mai!

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:10.240
I'm well aware that you're the 
dependable older sister type,

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:14.510
but it's okay to act spoiled once in a while.

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:15.700
Ellen-chan?

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:24.190
Mai?

00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:27.020
Thank you, Dad!

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.380
The presence disappeared?

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:45.820
Okay. So we're giving 
up on the transfer, then.

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:50.430
You accepted that rather easily.
 You're not concerned?

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:55.250
Of course I'm concerned, but I 
sensed it would turn out like this.

00:20:55.970 --> 00:21:00.140
After all, my dear, you're 
awfully soft on Mai.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:06.990
Ugh, another Japanese meal?

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:11.310
Why don't you like it?
 Mai-oneechan's cooking is so delicious.

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:14.740
Like I said, I prefer toast.

00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:16.490
Stop complaining and eat.

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:18.420
Yes, yes.

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:21.570
Only say "yes" once, right?

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:22.620
Mom!

00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:24.660
You're up early today.

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:28.900
Yes, I wanted to eat the breakfast Mai made.

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:30.390
You, too, Dad?

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:31.220
Yes.

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:33.200
And not just coffee?

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:34.140
Yes.

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:36.390
Is that all right, Mai?

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:37.900
Of course!

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:12.860
<b>Ayanokouji Martial Arts School</b>

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:23.050
You are back late, Princess.

00:23:25.980 --> 00:23:26.890
Yomi...

00:23:29.030 --> 00:23:30.460
Excuse me.

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:39.890
<b>Next Episode  Slothful Person's Honor</b>
